backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/**/__pycache__/
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
# Hand-made copies of the farm database (boord.db.bak-*, boord.db.realmaster-*).
# Same data as boord.db, so the same rule: never one `git add -A` from GitHub.
data/boord.db.*
data/.secret_key
data/release_key.fpr
# Written by update_server.bat with the tag it checked out. Only a fallback
# for backend/version.py when git cannot answer - but it describes this one
# install, so it does not belong in the repository.
data/installed_version.txt
# Written by "update_server.bat --check" - what the last check for a newer
# signed release found. Describes this install's position, not the code.
data/update_available.json
data/update_available.tmp
# Nothing writes this any more - Boord has no accounts, and install.ps1
# deletes any copy an older install left behind. The line stays
# because a farm that has not re-run the installer yet still has the file, and
# only named paths under data/ are ignored, not data/ itself: without it that
# password sits one `git add -A` away from being pushed to GitHub.
data/initial_admin_password.txt
# Written by watchdog.ps1 - what it found and restarted on this one PC. The
# watchdog moved to Boord Monitor in its 2.0 (its log is in that folder now);
# these stay ignored because a farm's old files are still here.
data/watchdog.log
data/watchdog.log.1
# Hand-made to tell the watchdog to leave the servers alone while somebody
# is working on them.
data/watchdog.pause
data/imports/
data/photos/
data/backups/
data/reports/
# The farm Gmail's address and app password (market_mail.py): a credential.
data/market_mail.txt
# The market invoices read from that Gmail, and the fetch log.
data/market_mail/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
# The heartbeat's ping URLs, before the heartbeat moved to Boord Monitor
# (its data\heartbeat_url.txt now). A credential: keep it ignored.
heartbeat_url.txt
NEXT_STEPS.md
# Working file for the admin training deck - the PDFs are what ship.
Boord_Admin_Training.pptx
